  "answer": "This has been reported before. PowerToys#43161 is the main ticket. PowerToys Backup and restore doesn't include Command Palette settings, and it doesn't detect changes made in Command Palette. Commenters there are asking for the feature, and the archive shows no fix yet. In the meantime, copy the Command Palette settings folder by hand. It's hidden by default, at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Packages\\Microsoft.CommandPalette_8wekyb3d8bbwe\\LocalState. It holds the settings files and extension data such as bookmarks.json. Some installs may use %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Microsoft.CmdPal instead. Copy that folder somewhere safe, and copy it back after reinstalling or moving to another PC. PowerToys#40372 describes the same workaround for bookmarks. Add a thumbs-up or a comment to PowerToys#43161 to support the request."
